      },
      "message": "fix(motion): Face opens with an approach rapid on the clearance plane\n\nThe facer started its path at the entry point in the air, so its first\nmove was the plunge. Posts write a move's end only, so the first posted\nmotion was a 3-axis feed from the tool-change position straight to cutting\ndepth. Face now starts its cursor where the other mill generators do and\nrapids to the entry at clearance before the plunge. An entry at exactly\nX0 Y0 states that approach as a zero-length rapid.\n\nGoldens regenerated: the face .cl goldens and every dialect's .nc\n(including program_entry pause/home) gain the G00 approach; regression\nmove/line counts and minutes take the one extra rapid; the fixture-law\ntest names the approach beside the plunge.\n\nFixes #690\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
